## 2026-11-11 — Databricks CLI install + MCP client example (connectivity only)

Task: user supplied a Databricks AI Gateway MCP notebook snippet
(`system.ai.github` MCP service) and asked to log in with the Databricks CLI and
run it locally.

- Installed Databricks CLI v1.26.0 to `d:\breakdown\.tools\databricks-cli\databricks.exe`
  from the official GitHub release artifact (same URL winget uses; SHA-256
  verified against the published digest `7c7f2bdf…14a2`). Added to the user PATH.
  Reason: `databricks` was not installed; winget install attempts kept being
  interrupted by the terminal-capture issue, so the release zip was fetched via a
  detached background download instead. Untracked build artifacts (`.tools/`)
  are outside repo source.
- Added `examples/databricks_mcp_list_tools.py`: local adaptation of the snippet,
  verified against the project `.venv` dependency set (mcp==2.3.0,
  httpx2==2.16.0). mcp 2.3.0's `streamable_http_client` yields a 2-tuple and
  requires an `httpx2.AsyncClient`, so the snippet's API usage was correct for
  this repo (no v1.x-style `get_session_id` third element). Robust CLI lookup
  (PATH or `.tools` fallback), `--host` on `auth token` (required in
  non-interactive environments), and an actionable error when OAuth is not yet
  configured.
  Reason: user-requested connectivity example; no secrets hardcoded.

Verification: `ruff check` passes; script executes and fails only at the expected
pre-auth step with the CLI's own message ("databricks OAuth is not configured for
this host … run `databricks auth login`"). End-to-end tool listing is pending the
interactive `databricks auth login` (browser), which only the user can complete.

Not done / deviations: no dependency or workflow-file changes; the snippet's
`%pip install` notebook line is not applicable locally (mcp/httpx2 already
present in `.venv`).

