## 2026-11-11 (addendum) — Fix "model list shows none": align Cline modal settings

Diagnosis: the Cline model dropdown is built from `baseUrl + GET /models`; the
selected model id was absent from that list because settings disagreed with
each other and with the endpoint. Two state files carry the selection and the
running Cline UI rewrites them on interaction (observed apiKey prefix and model
id change between consecutive reads), so alignment required editing both.

- Changed (outside repo, user-invited fix): `~/.cline/data/settings/providers.json`
  → `providers.modal.settings.baseUrl` repointed from the Qwen endpoint to
  `https://cs1508-4ever-oneshot--ep-glm-5-3-flash-nvfp4-server.us-west.modal.direct/v1`
  and `.model` set to `nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4`.
- Changed (outside repo): `~/.cline/data/globalState.json` → `planModeApiModelId`
  and `actModeApiModelId` set to `nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4`; providers remain `modal`.
- Reason: make label, dropdown list, and serving weights agree on the cheaper
  GLM deployment (user goal: lower cost, same API).
- Verification: `/models` under stored key returns exactly the selected id
  (membership True for providers.json and both globalState mode ids); live
  chat completion through the corrected config returned 'ok' then 'ready'.
- Auth note: both credential schemes verified equivalent for this endpoint —
  User-scope env `MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_ID`+`MODAL_PROXY_TOKEN_SECRET` composed as
  `id.secret`, and the stored `wk-` web key; each lists the same single model.
- Caveat: the running Cline UI may rewrite these files on its next settings
  interaction; if the list empties again, re-align or reselect after reload.

